      "id": "DLM-01",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "A translated pair gives a uniform primal minimum",
      "anchor": "inputs-dual-primal",
      "statement": "For every positive h, λ(ret μ h)≥min(1/16,1/(1024 r C₁₆)). A suitable single scale suffices whenever the base term is small.",
      "hypotheses": "Number field L, N≥1, a smoothing μ of λ∨, r the number of infinite places, and the uniform lattice count factor C₁₆ for a dilation of squared radii by 16. The primal estimate does not require L totally complex.",
      "definitions": [
        "q_h is squared length, summed once per infinite place. θ equals one up to 1 and equals zero from 4 onwards.",
        "The one-scale term at d=4ʲ is a weighted sum of outer products divided by d² times the sum of the weights. Its outer cutoff is θ(dμ).",
        "For u realizing the corrected primal minimum set a=q_h(u). The inner ball has squared radius d/4."
      ],
      "equations": [
        "inputs-dual-primal-bound"
      ],
